1
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,120
Proper.

2
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,600
Oh!

3
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:08,120
I said I'd make you your birthday breakfast.

4
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:11,080
Yeah, well, I was hungry and you were dead to the world.

5
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,280
Sorry.

6
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,120
Truckload of presents should make up for that.

7
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,240
- Yeah, about that... - I'm joking!

8
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,280
- No presents. Just a cake. - Yeah.

9
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:22,880
- You have got me a cake? - Yeah, I'm all over the cake.

10
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,040
Mm. Now there's an image!

11
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:34,160
All right, Monday, Do your worst.

12
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:35,440
- Mwah. - Mwah.

13
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:37,040
- Have a great day. - I will.

14
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:56,680
Whoa! You all right, love?

15
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:58,600
Hello! Hello!

16
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,080
Hello, pooch.

17
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,040
- Have a leaflet. - All right. Thanks.

18
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,360
- Morning. Have one of these. - Thanks.

19
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:04,880
Hi. You all right?

20
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,920
Morning, Reggie.

21
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:18,400
Hello, good morning. First time in Gloucester?

22
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,640
Try my guided tour.

23
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,800
First time in Gloucester?

24
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:24,000
Is this your first time in Gloucester? Try my guided tour!

25
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,960
This is me. Try my guided tour.

26
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,840
I know all the exciting facts about Gloucester yes, I do.

27
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,440
Test me!

28
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,640
Go on, then.

29
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:34,720
- Tell me something. - OK.

30
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:37,760
In 1216, the cathedral hosted

31
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,640
the coronation of King Henry III,

32
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,080
and he was only nine at the time!

33
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:46,080
They filmed Harry Potter here, too.

34
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:49,320
Yeah, well, plenty more where that came from.

35
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,880
Tours start at 10.00, 12.00, and 2.00.

36
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,400
I'll... think about it.

37
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,960
Yeah.

38
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:56,760
She won't think about it.

39
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,520
No, dear, she won't.

40
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,440
Oh, well. Never mind.

41
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:02,040
Day's still young.

42
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,400
It's meant to be a heart.

43
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,480
Er... needs work.

44
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:13,520
I know. Man spends his entire life behind a bar...

45
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:16,960
...pivoting to the cafe trade ain't easy, but I try.

46
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,760
For you, I'd try anything.

47
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,880
Allan, we've talked about this.

48
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,880
Oh, I know you're with Lee, but you deserve better!

49
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:25,920
Oh.

50
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:28,200
You know there's something wrong there.

51
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:32,640
Is that an actual dossier?

52
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:35,400
- Yes, on Lee. My Lee dossier. - Oh, come on!

53
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,120
He hardly talk to anyone...

54
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,800
...cuts his own hair,

55
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,800
gets weird books out from the library,

56
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,640
claims that his family's from round here

57
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:44,400
but I can't find anyone who knew them.

58
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,440
- How can you trust that? - Thank you for my birthday coffee.

59
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,360
Ruth, I'm telling you, I hear things.

60
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,600
They don't call me All Ears Allan for nothin'.

61
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:55,240
It's not a nickname if you give it to yourself, is it?

62
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:25,200
Ko Fro Lo!

63
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Bo Fro Sho To!

64
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,480
No Bo Ko!

65
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,400
Mo Lo So!

66
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,840
No Kro Do!

67
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,520
She's doing it again.

68
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,120
Spending hours at the controls looking for something.

69
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,000
Thinks we haven't noticed.

70
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,920
I'll ask her.

71
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:04,560
Hey, Doc, what are you looking for?

72
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,480
How long have you been there?

73
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,720
20 minutes.

74
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,280
You haven't.

75
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,360
What you looking for?

76
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,640
Not looking for anything.

77
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:14,120
Don't lie to us.

78
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,000
The Master.

79
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,720
Why would you do that?

80
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,680
- The Kasaavin took him. - Yes.

81
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,120
They transported him to their dimension

82
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,480
and I can't get there in the TARDIS, but I thought...

83
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,360
...if he escaped, I could track him.

84
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:33,280
There's no sign.

85
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:35,640
I thought he'd be the last person you'd want to see.

86
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,600
He left a message for me.

87
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,440
Saying what?

88
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,840
It's personal.

89
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:46,960
Is that where you go?

90
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,560
When you leave us to explore and you say

91
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,640
you'll be back in an hour but you never are?

92
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,120
Are you out looking for him?

93
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,640
Where do you go?

94
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,760
Home.

95
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,600
On my own.

96
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,600
Why? Why not with us?

97
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,600
Cos you ask too many questions.

98
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,600
Maybe because we're worried about you?

99
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,840
I mean, one minute you're all smiles,

100
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,720
next minute your mind's somewhere else.

101
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:33,880
Kro Kro Tro Kro So Fro So So To!

102
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,880
- Kro Kro Tro Kro... - What is that?

103
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,840
A Judoon warning transmission.

104
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:40,600
The cheek!

105
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,960
Judoon?

106
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:43,520
Are you just saying that to shut us up?

107
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:46,080
Dangerous intergalactic police for hire.

108
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:50,120
Notice... of a zonal enforcement field on Earth,

109
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,800
no-one can get in or out.

110
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:55,680
What? They're preparing to beam down there.

111
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:58,120
A platoon of Judoon. Near the moon.

112
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,720
They can't do that. They've got no jurisdiction there.

113
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:04,040
Right in the centre of Gloucester! I am not having that!

114
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:06,400
If I can match the TARDIS's rotation

115
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:09,600
to the frequency of the enforcement field's refresh rate,

116
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:10,800
I might just might be able

117
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,600
to slip us in before anyone gets killed.

118
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,040
I thought you said they were the police.

119
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,960
Trigger-happy police.

120
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,680
Do Po Lo Sho!

121
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,920
No Dro Fo Ro! Zo!

122
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,160
To Fo Ro!

123
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,840
Dro Ro Fro!

124
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:42,840
Bo.

125
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:45,680
Dro!

126
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,200
So Zo Ro!

127
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,880
To Sho Fro!

128
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,600
So Zo To!

129
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,600
No Fo Lo!

130
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,840
No Fo Lo!

131
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,920
No Fo Bo Bo Lo!

132
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,320
Ro!

133
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:14,920
Bo Ro Kro To Fro Bo! Zo!

134
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:18,160
- Marcia, don't! - How dare you!

135
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:22,120
This is a peaceful, small city. Who even are you?

136
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,080
Tro Ko Sho.

137
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,920
That took me nine weeks.

138
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,160
That took me nine weeks.

139
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,800
Language, human.

140
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,680
What's this?

141
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,760
Compensation for your weapon.

142
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,560
Answer her question!

143
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,080
Who are you?

144
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,800
We are...

145
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:44,280
...the Judoon.

146
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:49,000
Oh... my... God!

147
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,600
You will be catalogued.

148
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:53,520
I will not! Stay away from me!

149
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,280
No! Marcia!

150
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:01,600
Enforcement field perimeter at maximum strength.

151
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,840
You killed her!

152
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:06,280
Category, human.

153
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,160
Fugitive match, negative.

154
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:13,040
- What do you want with us? - All within the perimeter

155
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:16,480
must be catalogued. The fugitive is here.

156
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,200
Well, look who it isn't...!

157
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,640
I've come to get the cake

158
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:25,600
that I've ordered for Ruth's birthday.

159
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,680
Oh, got it right here.

160
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:28,760
A special birthday message to her.

161
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:36,320
What is the matter with you? Why don't you let it go?

162
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,520
You want to take this outside?

163
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:38,520
Stop asking me that

164
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:40,760
every time I come in here for a latte!

165
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,600
Humans!

166
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:45,600
- Through here. - What are you doing in my kitchen?!

167
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:48,360
Stay inside. Keep the door closed. Do not let anyone in,

168
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:51,200
especially alien police in helmets and black leather.

169
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:54,720
The city's under siege. We're going to sort it.

170
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:58,360
Oh, yeah, go on, get out. Coward!

171
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:00,240
- What is up with him? - How long you got?

172
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:02,840
No time at all. Stay inside. Lock the door.

173
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,160
Come on, gang, no time.

174
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:07,560
No, no, guys, look at this little lot.

175
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:08,680
Lovely!

176
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,080
Look at the state of that!

177
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,640
That's the worst cake I've ever seen!

178
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,320
Ruth, I've been looking everywhere for you.

179
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,600
- Have you seen? - Yeah.

180
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,880
- They're aliens! - I know, I know.

181
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:23,120
Real aliens. They killed Marcia.

182
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,320
- What? - Marcia's dead.

183
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,560
We need to get home. Now.

184
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:31,360
Space rhinos?

185
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,560
I've got no money. I'm sorry, I'm terrible at this job.

186
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:38,880
Category, human. Fugitive match, negative.

187
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,280
Oh, you're after a fugitive?

188
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,760
I can help. He just left.

189
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:44,200
On the counter, there's a dossier.

190
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,360
It's really thorough.

191
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:51,240
Hey! Watch it, you big... lunk!

192
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:56,320
Sorry.

193
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,480
Assaulting an officer.

194
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,720
Sentence, execution.

195
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,920
Sentence complete!

196
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,600
OK.

197
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:08,880
Need to grab some essentials, a few clothes. We need to go.

198
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,680
What are you talking about? Go where?

199
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:12,120
Do you trust me, Ruth?

200
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,120
Sometimes.

201
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:16,240
You need to just do what I say.

202
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:18,240
Just get some clothes and put them in a suitcase.

203
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,640
They can't be after you. They're aliens.

204
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:22,440
They've got the heads of rhinos.

205
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:24,160
You're from Stroud, Lee.

206
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,960
If there's something I need to know,

207
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,840
you tell me right now.

208
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,800
There's no time. Come on.

209
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:43,160
Fugitive house unit located.

210
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,600
Prepare isolator.

211
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:46,720
I hope you've got a permit for that.

212
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:48,720
You're an Imperial Regulator?

213
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:51,440
Yes. And there's plenty here to regulate.

214
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,760
For starters, you don't have jurisdiction here.

215
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:57,080
So, why you're using a Class Seven Enforcement Field

216
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:59,080
around this city bothers me a lot.

217
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,840
More importantly, this temporal isolator

218
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,680
is an outlawed piece of kit.

219
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:06,720
Radiation leakage and civilian casualties.

220
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,200
Designed to freeze time but causes

221
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,480
horrific collateral damage to anything and anyone

222
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,400
that gets in its path. Horrible thing.

223
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,120
Hey, you're not using that thing here, pal,

224
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:16,840
so consider your rhino backside imperially regulated.

225
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,760
It sounded tougher in me head.

226
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:23,560
Fugitive is highly dangerous. Precautions must be taken.

227
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,720
Not that weapon, not here.

228
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:27,600
Humans will die, and you,

229
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:29,680
Captain, will have racked up enough violations

230
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:31,880
to ensure that your troop never get hired again.

231
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:36,760
Look at you and your platoon of Judoon near the...

232
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,800
...that lagoon.

233
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:39,960
More of a canal.

234
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,720
- Yeah. - Where's your pride?

235
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:45,000
Where's your respect for the rules?

236
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,880
I'm very disappointed in you.

237
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,040
So, we will take over from here.

238
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,320
Negative!

239
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:54,000
Mission must be fulfilled by the contracted troop.

240
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,280
Judoon Engagement Article 163B!

241
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:59,520
That article... is overridden

242
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,400
by local Earth law...

243
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:03,760
...12...

244
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:06,600
...which clearly states that any potential arrestee

245
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:09,080
is entitled to arbitration with a third party.

246
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:12,440
Isn't that correct, Liaison Officer Khan?

247
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:14,800
Absolutely correct. 100%.

248
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,960
Rule 12? Massive.

249
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:18,520
Imperial regulation.

250
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:22,280
So, you will give us the time to go in there and arbitrate.

251
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:24,320
That weapon will not need to be used.

252
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:26,000
Clear?

253
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:29,480
Come on! We can sort this, woman to woman.

254
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:32,240
Give me ten Earth minutes

255
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:33,720
and we can have this resolved for you.

256
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,320
Five minutes.

257
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,480
Nine. Four!

258
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:39,280
Er, fine. I'll take five.

259
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:40,960
I hate it when they do that.

260
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:43,480
We'd best take the lift. Hang on, where's Graham?

261
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:45,160
- I don't know. - Have you lost him?!

262
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:46,680
He's not my responsibility.

263
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:48,720
He's always a few steps behind. I've stopped checking.

264
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:49,880
Four minutes 30.

265
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:52,280
We haven't started yet! Come on.

266
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,240
Don't move.

267
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,480
Seriously, not a muscle.

268
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:13,560
Working on the movement sensors.

269
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:16,480
If you even flinch, it'll set off the laser spikes.

270
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:19,240
Trust me, they get everywhere.

271
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:21,720
By the way, lookin' good.

272
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:24,760
Who is this? What's going on?

273
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:26,320
Where am I? And where are you?

274
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:29,080
Neutralised.

275
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,160
Comin' to join you.

276
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:33,600
You can get excited now.

277
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:37,000
Ha! You missed me, right?

278
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:40,280
Ha-ha!

279
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:46,880
Have we met?

280
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:50,280
Still cheeky. Regeneration can't change that.

281
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,960
Got to say, loving the grey at the temple.

282
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:55,560
Kind of distinguished yet still sexy.

283
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:58,000
- Oh, come here! - Whoa!

284
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:02,320
How you been, Doctor?

285
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,640
Ah.

286
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:09,280
Pay attention, cos every word I'm about to say is true.

287
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,760
There's a nasty bunch of alien police outside.

288
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:14,800
They're pointing a highly dangerous cannon at this flat,

289
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:17,680
and they'll fire it in about, er, four minutes.

290
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:20,080
I might be able to stop them, but I need to understand

291
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:22,880
exactly why they're here, so you need to let us in, quick.

292
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,400
Right, tell us everything.

293
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,840
Who are you? We need to leave!

294
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,160
Right into the arms of intergalactic mercenaries

295
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:34,400
who seem to think you are a fugitive from justice.

296
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:36,240
- They've got it wrong. - Sure about that?

297
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,800
Yeah! It's mistaken identity.

298
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,240
He works at Bathrooms4U, for God's sake!

299
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:42,840
You'd better be telling the truth, both of you,

300
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:44,560
otherwise the Judoon will have you

301
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:47,520
for harbouring the fugitive, and their justice is brutal.

302
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,440
I'm not harbouring anyone!

303
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:52,080
If you're both so innocent, why are your bags packed?

304
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,640
Yeah, like you're about to go on the run.

305
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:55,760
Khan and Sinclair with the key questions.

306
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,120
Not that you'll get very far,

307
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,560
given the enforcement perimeter they've just knocked up.

308
00:15:59,560 --> 00:16:00,800
Come on, quick with the truth!

309
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:03,160
We've got about three minutes, probably less.

310
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:04,840
What are you hiding?

311
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,600
Check the flat, see what's here.

312
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:08,840
If it isn't these two, it could be something inside here.

313
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:10,960
- You're not going through my flat! - Yes, they are.

314
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:12,400
Have you seen those things outside?

315
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,960
Yeah, and I've seen what they do,

316
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:15,120
and that's why we're running.

317
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,400
What are you doing?

318
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:19,000
- What is that?! - A device that tells me...

319
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,840
...you're both completely human.

320
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:30,840
Please, I'm trying to save a lot of lives here, including yours.

321
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:33,520
If you have any idea why the Judoon are pursuing you,

322
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:35,440
you have to tell me right now.

323
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:43,200
What the...? What's happening out there?

324
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,920
I guess they want their ship back.

325
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,160
What, this ain't your ship?

326
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:47,600
You think I'd choose this look?

327
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:49,240
Doesn't even have a bar!

328
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:52,080
A little evasive action.

329
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:55,640
Hoping these shields are as good as they say.

330
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,640
A few battles going on around us...

331
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:02,280
You're not just kidding me? You're really not the Doctor?

332
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:05,160
Oh, no, no. My name's Graham. I just travel with the Doc.

333
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:08,600
Ha! Which is why the scoop read the wrong signal!

334
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:10,360
Ho-ho, using the old Quanticum Scoop

335
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,960
I got from a fourple on Ibiza 13... Whoo!

336
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,080
That was a night!

337
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:17,320
Actually, that was a month.

338
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:19,480
Well, look, now you know who I am, tell me who you are,

339
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,920
why you've kidnapped me and why you're after the Doc.

340
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,880
I mean, we're in the middle of something right now.

341
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:26,280
Captain Jack Harkness at your service.

342
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:28,400
Me and the Doc, we go way back.

343
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:29,720
This is important.

344
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:33,000
He needs to know the future of the universe is at stake.

345
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,360
Not he, she.

346
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,160
Oh!

347
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:40,040
This I gotta see.

348
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,880
Temporal isolator primed, Captain.

349
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,880
Prepare Final Warning Missile.

350
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:49,240
Find anything?

351
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,560
A few cash-flow problems,

352
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:52,640
a collection of old phones and keys.

353
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:54,280
I found this in the bedroom.

354
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,480
Hollow compartment at the back of the wardrobe.

355
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,120
And that...

356
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:00,520
...is not from Earth.

357
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:02,040
So where's it from?

358
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:06,160
- Oh, my God! - What was that?!

359
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:08,120
Just came flying through the window.

360
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:10,640
Isolation of fugitive housing unit

361
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:12,200
in 108 seconds.

362
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,600
Doesn't time fly when you don't have all the answers?

363
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:16,800
So, anyone know what this is?

364
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:18,160
No, I've never seen it before.

365
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,840
Me neither.

366
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,640
We found it hidden in your bedroom.

367
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:24,880
You'd better be telling the truth,

368
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,360
cos there's a lot of innocent people

369
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:28,280
that could die if we don't sort this out quick.

370
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:29,760
92 seconds.

371
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,160
Give me the box.

372
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:39,960
82 seconds.

373
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,800
Give me the box.

374
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:44,520
- Lee? What is that? - It's nothing.

375
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:46,800
No, it clearly is something,

376
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,760
cos suddenly you're all bothered about it,

377
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:50,400
and I've never seen it before in my life.

378
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:53,680
You're in charge, right?

379
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:55,360
It's a very flat team structure.

380
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:57,960
You're the smartest. I can see it in your eyes.

381
00:18:57,960 --> 00:19:01,120
Use the fire exit out the back. Take Ruth.

382
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:03,200
Get her out and make sure she's OK.

383
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,440
I can take care of this.

384
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:05,920
What? No, you can't!

385
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:08,080
What's in the box, Lee? Who are you really?

386
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:09,320
It's none of your business.

387
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,560
You've got half of Gloucester under Judoon lockdown.

388
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:15,920
I'm making it my business.

389
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,280
45 seconds.

390
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:19,680
I can deal with this.

391
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:22,000
Just take Ruth.

392
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,400
40 seconds.

393
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,440
Look, I've... I've made a mistake.

394
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:29,240
You're the most important thing in my life.

395
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:31,480
I can't let others lose their lives.

396
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,280
I need to make sure you're safe.

397
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:36,640
- What do you mean, "a mistake"? - I just need to talk to them, OK?

398
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:38,080
But they're space rhinos, Lee.

399
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:39,480
What are you going to chat to them about?

400
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:40,640
23 seconds.

401
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:42,680
They'll see us getting out of the fire escape.

402
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:44,360
- Unless... - Diversion!

403
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,720
Look, you take Ruth. We'll go out the front

404
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:46,840
and distract the space feds.

405
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,040
- You think that'll work? - Come on!

406
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,600
No, cos I'm not going anywhere without Lee.

407
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,640
I'm a police officer. I speak their language.

408
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,720
A bit of stalling, buy time to get them away.

409
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:55,920
Then we can come inside with them and be by your side.

410
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,360
I don't need you to be here.

411
00:19:57,360 --> 00:20:00,160
You obviously do, because there's a cannon about to fire at your flat.

412
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:03,640
Time limit exceeded. Initiating temporal isolation.

413
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,720
We're out of time.

414
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,440
It's the best plan we've got for keeping this block safe.

415
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,000
Right, be careful.

416
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,400
The Judoon might look dumb, but they're deadly.

417
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:12,560
Go to the cathedral. I'll meet you there. OK?

418
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:15,600
- You better. - Not going to miss your birthday, am I?

419
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:18,200
Go, go, before they launch that thing.

420
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:19,680
...full documentation available on request.

421
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:21,000
See you at the cathedral.

422
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:23,080
Activate Temporal Blast.

423
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,520
Stop!

424
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,240
Arbitration complete.

425
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,720
Arbitration result?

426
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,040
You can come in now.

427
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:33,120
So long as you turn that off.

428
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:36,080
Pause isolation. Remain here.

429
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:38,440
No fugitives in there, by the way.

430
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:43,480
And as for you lot, I don't want you using that.

431
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,400
Keeping my promise.

432
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:01,120
Surrender!

433
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:03,840
This property now under Judoon jurisdiction.

434
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:09,400
I surrender. OK?

435
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:12,680
You can tell your boss. You got me.

436
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:18,400
- Graham! - What just happened?

437
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,800
What are we doing here?

438
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:24,120
Short answers, this guy, stolen ship, being fired at.

439
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:26,400
We need to get back. And who are you?

440
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,720
Young. I like you young.

441
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:31,760
But silver fox said, "She, not he."

442
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:35,120
So you, not you, right?

443
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:37,680
I hope you kept the receipt for the scoop.

444
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:39,760
Seriously? Three of you?

445
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:41,520
I had a dream about this once.

446
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:42,920
Whoa!

447
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:44,880
Hold on to something.

448
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:49,120
Incoming matter transmission.

449
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:52,440
Commander Gat, your presence is not required.

450
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:54,680
Could've fooled me. I've been watching it all.

451
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:55,960
You're so noisy.

452
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:57,880
Talk about sledgehammers to crack a nut.

453
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:05,280
Presenting occupant of housing unit.

454
00:22:05,320 --> 00:22:07,360
Hello, old friend.

455
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:09,040
I see you're back from the dead.

456
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:12,400
We had such a moving funeral for you.

457
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:15,360
But I suppose that was your intention.

458
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:19,120
Did you really think that we wouldn't find you?

459
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,800
Did you think that I'd ever stop looking?

460
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:27,480
Good place to hide, mind, the far backside of a tiny galaxy.

461
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:29,640
How did you find me?

462
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:36,400
Sentiment was always going to be your downfall.

463
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:37,960
You kept it.

464
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:39,000
Silly.

465
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:41,000
Chronotelluric alloy, strong entanglement.

466
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:44,040
Very trackable. It just takes a while.

467
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:50,000
Yeah, well...

468
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,600
...I wanted to repair it...

469
00:22:53,520 --> 00:22:54,640
...polish it.

470
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:56,840
My service medal.

471
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:59,440
Honour and courage still mean something.

472
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,560
I agree.

473
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,640
See, this is the problem with our identical training.

474
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:08,320
We share all the same tricks.

475
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:10,880
Kill him.

476
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:14,880
Detained fugitive must be transferred to contracted...

477
00:23:14,880 --> 00:23:16,200
No, idiot.

478
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:18,520
- You didn't scan him yet, did you? - Uh-uh.

479
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:21,160
Bless.

480
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:28,600
Fugitive, negative. Explain.

481
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:31,080
I'm sorry it has to end this way.

482
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:33,040
You got so close to escaping.

483
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,880
Faithful companion.

484
00:23:40,360 --> 00:23:43,160
Do I have to spell it out for you?

485
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,360
All clear.

486
00:23:56,720 --> 00:23:59,000
Now, you need to tell me everything you know about Lee,

487
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:02,080
how long you've been together, and what was that metallic box?

488
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:03,440
Er...

489
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:07,560
_

490
00:24:13,520 --> 00:24:15,040
- Is that from Lee? - No.

491
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:17,320
It's... nothing.

492
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:25,480
This cathedral is under Judoon control.

493
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:28,640
All occupants must surrender immediately.

494
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:31,000
There will be no escape this time.

495
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:33,080
We have you surrounded!

496
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:38,880
- How can I help? - You interfered, Regulator.

497
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:40,320
You know what they say,

498
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:43,080
one person's arbitration is another person's interference.

499
00:24:43,080 --> 00:24:44,480
Very blurry line.

500
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,320
This is a place of worship.

501
00:24:47,320 --> 00:24:49,720
Show some respect, or I'll overload

502
00:24:49,720 --> 00:24:51,840
those guns and make it a bad day for everyone.

503
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:55,560
Now, let's go, and nobody needs to get hurt.

504
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:57,120
What have you done with Lee?

505
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:59,240
Information request granted.

506
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:04,200
Sentence, execution.

507
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,800
You murdered him.

508
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:11,040
That is a violation of your contract!

509
00:25:11,040 --> 00:25:12,480
Incorrect.

510
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:15,240
Contract stated retrieval of fugitive.

511
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:17,640
Fugitive identified.

512
00:25:20,600 --> 00:25:23,280
- What? - Biological shielding decrypted.

513
00:25:23,920 --> 00:25:25,360
Fugitive, positive.

514
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:36,600
That's it. Back up or Daddy Rhinoform gets it!

515
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:39,640
What are you doing?!

516
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:41,880
It feels like... instinct

517
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,720
against the bullies.

518
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:46,480
Cos you know the thing about bullies?

519
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:48,200
There's always a weak spot.

520
00:25:51,560 --> 00:25:54,160
Bo! Ko! Fo! Jo! To!

521
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,360
Do you know what you've just done?

522
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:04,520
Who are you?!

523
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:15,480
You have to get us back there. The Doctor needs us.

524
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:18,080
Listen, kid, working with some low-rent equipment here.

525
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:19,440
Why doesn't that surprise me?

526
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:22,080
Oh, she likes them mouthy, then, huh?

527
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,480
Yeah, one up from cheesy.

528
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:26,720
OK, he's my favourite.

529
00:26:28,560 --> 00:26:29,800
Whoo!

530
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:32,120
Why didn't it scoop her? Why can't I get her here?

531
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:37,160
Are there Judoon anywhere near where I scooped you?

532
00:26:37,160 --> 00:26:38,760
Yeah! A lot.

533
00:26:38,760 --> 00:26:40,640
Oh, I knew it!

534
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:41,760
Level Seven Enforcement Field.

535
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:44,200
That's why I can't get accurate traces on her.

536
00:26:44,200 --> 00:26:46,040
Interfering with everything.

537
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:49,000
Is she safe?

538
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:05,360
Total Judoon evacuation.

539
00:27:07,520 --> 00:27:09,960
They've even removed the enforcement perimeter.

540
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:11,880
That's got to be good?

541
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:14,200
No! Judoon switching strategy

542
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:16,960
means things have got very bad and very personal now.

543
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:18,520
Ruth...

544
00:27:18,520 --> 00:27:20,720
...you just dishonoured a Judoon captain,

545
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:23,640
and removing their horn is the worst insult.

546
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:27,040
I think you know far more than you're telling me

547
00:27:27,080 --> 00:27:30,360
about Lee and about why the Judoon are here.

548
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:31,960
It's time to share.

549
00:27:31,960 --> 00:27:33,880
I don't know anything.

550
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:37,760
I don't even know how I did what I just did to them.

551
00:27:40,120 --> 00:27:42,800
I don't have the decryption for your bio-shield.

552
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:45,960
You and Lee must have both had them.

553
00:27:45,960 --> 00:27:50,040
Very sophisticated, like biological cloaking.

554
00:27:51,080 --> 00:27:52,320
Look at me.

555
00:27:52,320 --> 00:27:54,240
I know my own life.

556
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:57,080
I'm Ruth Clayton.

557
00:27:57,080 --> 00:27:58,720
I am 44.

558
00:27:58,720 --> 00:28:00,280
I'm married.

559
00:28:00,280 --> 00:28:01,800
I'm a tour guide.

560
00:28:01,800 --> 00:28:03,560
And I am scared!

561
00:28:04,560 --> 00:28:06,240
Back then...

562
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:07,560
...that was not me.

563
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:09,960
My hands, they just moved. They...

564
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:11,960
Well, if it wasn't you, who was it?

565
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:13,240
I don't know.

566
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:16,760
I don't understand any of this. None of this is me. It can't be.

567
00:28:17,720 --> 00:28:18,760
Help me.

568
00:28:20,600 --> 00:28:22,320
Show me your phone.

569
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:25,280
You received a message just before you turned into Jackie Chan.

570
00:28:25,280 --> 00:28:28,240
"Follow the light. Break the glass."

571
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:30,520
Ruth, I don't think you are

572
00:28:30,520 --> 00:28:33,320
who you say you are or who you think you are.

573
00:28:33,320 --> 00:28:36,600
I think there's another identity hidden within you.

574
00:28:38,120 --> 00:28:41,520
Maybe this text is an activation message...

575
00:28:41,560 --> 00:28:43,960
...words to trigger the real you,

576
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:46,600
the instincts that enabled you to attack the Judoon.

577
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:49,040
No. I'm not that person.

578
00:28:49,040 --> 00:28:50,680
I don't want to be that person.

579
00:28:50,680 --> 00:28:53,360
I'm afraid you don't have a choice!

580
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:55,840
Do you have any idea what this means?

581
00:28:55,840 --> 00:28:58,480
The light. The glass.

582
00:29:05,960 --> 00:29:07,400
Yeah, I do.

583
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:09,720
I just saw it.

584
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:12,280
But it's just a memory.

585
00:29:12,280 --> 00:29:13,400
A memory of what?

586
00:29:13,400 --> 00:29:16,680
The lighthouse where I grew up,

587
00:29:16,680 --> 00:29:18,200
my family home.

588
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:22,120
Why am I seeing that now?

589
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:24,480
I haven't thought about that for years.

590
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:26,000
It's something to do with this message.

591
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:29,360
He had to send it to you before the Judoon got to him.

592
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:31,160
What did he know?

593
00:29:32,040 --> 00:29:33,440
Are you sure it's your home?

594
00:29:33,440 --> 00:29:34,560
Of course I'm sure!

595
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:36,840
I know... where I was brought up.

596
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:40,240
My parents are buried there, on the land outside.

597
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:45,680
I haven't thought about them for years, either.

598
00:29:46,400 --> 00:29:48,960
- Do you know how to get there? - Course I do.

599
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:50,880
Then we're going, me and you, now.

600
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:55,480
Ship's security is fighting back.

601
00:29:56,080 --> 00:29:57,840
You gotta be kidding me!

602
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:00,960
Anti-theft attack system.

603
00:30:00,960 --> 00:30:03,720
Oh! Well, now I'm offended.

604
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:05,560
Look, guys, I'm sorry, I got get out of here.

605
00:30:05,560 --> 00:30:06,760
I got about a minute

606
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:09,520
before the ship's nanogenes attack my body.

607
00:30:09,520 --> 00:30:11,560
- What's going to happen to us? - Oh!

608
00:30:11,600 --> 00:30:14,080
I'll pre-set the coordinates to get you back.

609
00:30:15,120 --> 00:30:16,840
Just tell her this.

610
00:30:16,840 --> 00:30:18,720
I'm going to see her again.

611
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:20,320
Maybe not soon.

612
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:23,160
When she needs me, I'll be there.

613
00:30:23,160 --> 00:30:24,840
In the meantime...

614
00:30:24,840 --> 00:30:26,840
...tell her...

615
00:30:26,840 --> 00:30:29,600
...beware the lone Cyberman.

616
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:35,640
You don't know what a Cyberman is yet, do you?

617
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:37,200
No. What are they?

618
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:39,320
An empire of evil...

619
00:30:39,320 --> 00:30:41,080
...in ruins right now...

620
00:30:41,920 --> 00:30:45,120
...brought down to nothing...

621
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:46,360
...finally.

622
00:30:46,360 --> 00:30:48,640
But that could all change

623
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:50,920
if she doesn't listen to this message.

624
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:55,240
To defeat them, the alliance

625
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:59,840
sent this thing back through time, across space.

626
00:31:00,600 --> 00:31:02,800
Agh! Oh!

627
00:31:02,800 --> 00:31:05,000
They are coming for me!

628
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:07,960
Always the nanogenes!

629
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:12,840
I gotta go. I've set the scoop for return.

630
00:31:12,840 --> 00:31:15,280
It should take you back to where you were.

631
00:31:16,200 --> 00:31:18,200
Tell the Doctor...

632
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:20,160
...the lone Cyberman.

633
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:23,160
Don't give it what it wants.

634
00:31:23,160 --> 00:31:24,760
At all costs!

635
00:31:24,760 --> 00:31:26,320
Tell her!

636
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:29,120
We've lost him!

637
00:31:30,440 --> 00:31:32,000
Are we stuck here now?

638
00:31:35,520 --> 00:31:37,880
I hope he's got this thing right.

639
00:31:41,520 --> 00:31:43,200
Tell me about your parents.

640
00:31:43,200 --> 00:31:45,360
I wish I could tell you I adored them.

641
00:31:46,040 --> 00:31:49,200
But they chose to live in a disused lighthouse.

642
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:52,160
That tells you how good they were with people.

643
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:54,200
Not like you, in the heart of the city,

644
00:31:54,200 --> 00:31:55,800
talking to people all day long.

645
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:58,760
I guess we all rebel against our parents.

646
00:31:58,760 --> 00:32:00,280
It's part of growing up, innit?

647
00:32:00,280 --> 00:32:02,440
Never been a fan of growing up.

648
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:06,600
They loved it out here. Suited them.

649
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:08,840
Loved it so much they wanted to be buried here?

650
00:32:08,840 --> 00:32:11,320
- Yep. - You'd moved away by then.

651
00:32:11,320 --> 00:32:13,160
Yeah. But you still own the lighthouse?

652
00:32:13,160 --> 00:32:14,920
Yeah, they left it to me.

653
00:32:14,920 --> 00:32:17,800
But I never wanted to come back here to live, though.

654
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:22,760
When did you move to Gloucester?

655
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:26,440
Ooh... 1999.

656
00:32:26,440 --> 00:32:28,240
Mid-December.

657
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:32,160
Are you testing me?

658
00:32:33,280 --> 00:32:34,280
Yes.

659
00:32:34,920 --> 00:32:36,920
I don't know why I'm even trusting you.

660
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:38,840
I've got one of those faces.

661
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:41,920
I promise you...

662
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:44,360
...I'm your best hope of finding out who you are

663
00:32:44,360 --> 00:32:45,960
and staying alive.

664
00:32:50,800 --> 00:32:52,200
Ruth?

665
00:32:55,760 --> 00:32:58,400
What are you seeing or hearing?

666
00:32:58,440 --> 00:32:59,840
Nothing.

667
00:33:00,920 --> 00:33:02,480
We're nearly there.

668
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:20,480
That smell...

669
00:33:20,480 --> 00:33:22,000
...home.

670
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:26,960
Forgotten what it feels like to come back here.

671
00:33:27,840 --> 00:33:29,360
Like nothing can touch me.

672
00:33:30,760 --> 00:33:32,520
Mind if I take a look around?

673
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:37,440
Sure.

674
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:41,880
I'll get a fire going.

675
00:34:53,280 --> 00:34:55,240
Why have a blank gravestone?

676
00:35:00,400 --> 00:35:02,200
Because it's not a grave.

677
00:35:10,240 --> 00:35:13,200
Break the glass and follow the light.

678
00:35:13,200 --> 00:35:15,840
Break the glass and follow the light.

679
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:20,040
Break the glass and follow the light.

680
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:22,040
Break the glass and follow the light.

681
00:35:22,040 --> 00:35:24,320
Break the glass and...

682
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:09,280
You're probably a bit confused right now.

683
00:36:13,120 --> 00:36:15,080
I broke the glass.

684
00:36:15,080 --> 00:36:17,280
It's all come back to me.

685
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:19,640
This.

686
00:36:21,240 --> 00:36:22,840
What is this?

687
00:36:23,520 --> 00:36:25,160
That's my ship.

688
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,240
What?!

689
00:36:28,680 --> 00:36:30,280
Let me take it from the top.

690
00:36:31,040 --> 00:36:33,400
Hello, I'm The Doctor.

691
00:36:37,520 --> 00:36:40,400
I'm a traveller in space and time,

692
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:44,200
and that thing buried down there is called a TARDIS.

693
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:47,640
Time And Relative Dimension In Space.

694
00:36:47,680 --> 00:36:49,920
You're going to love this.

695
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:01,920
Come on, old girl.

696
00:37:01,920 --> 00:37:03,840
Too sleepy.

697
00:37:03,840 --> 00:37:05,240
Power up!

698
00:37:06,320 --> 00:37:07,720
Need you right now.

699
00:37:09,920 --> 00:37:13,000
Hi. Struggling with this. Can you just...?

700
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:15,600
No, I can't. Not right now. No time.

701
00:37:15,600 --> 00:37:18,240
Just stand there and don't ask questions.

702
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:20,640
Sorry you got caught up in all this,

703
00:37:20,640 --> 00:37:23,240
but if Gat is half the operative she used to be,

704
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:24,760
she's already figured out where we are.

705
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:27,320
And we need to be ready, and we're not.

706
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:28,640
Stop. Who's Gat?

707
00:37:28,640 --> 00:37:30,480
And who are you, really?

708
00:37:30,480 --> 00:37:31,680
Truly.

709
00:37:31,680 --> 00:37:33,480
I told you, love. I'm The Doctor.

710
00:37:33,480 --> 00:37:35,680
You can't be. Yeah? And why's that?

711
00:37:35,680 --> 00:37:37,400
Because I'm The Doctor.

712
00:37:39,920 --> 00:37:42,880
You have got to be kidding me!

713
00:37:44,160 --> 00:37:45,240
Really?

714
00:37:45,240 --> 00:37:46,480
Yes, really!

715
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:49,360
Since when? Since forever.

716
00:37:49,360 --> 00:37:51,520
And how did I end up like...

717
00:37:51,520 --> 00:37:52,720
...that?

718
00:37:52,720 --> 00:37:55,720
All rainbows and trousers that don't reach?

719
00:37:55,720 --> 00:37:57,880
What? No. How did I end up like you?

720
00:37:57,880 --> 00:38:01,520
You don't. You're in my future, not the other way round.

721
00:38:02,600 --> 00:38:04,440
I've never been anything like you.

722
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:06,480
Trust me, I'd remember. Especially that shirt.

723
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:08,960
So would I, if I'd ever been you, which I haven't.

724
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:10,440
What?

725
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:13,520
Huh?

726
00:38:14,520 --> 00:38:17,520
That's not possible. Unless it is.

727
00:38:17,520 --> 00:38:20,000
But what would that mean? Doesn't make sense.

728
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:21,240
Stop doing that!

729
00:38:21,240 --> 00:38:24,000
Oh. Same brain.

730
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:26,720
No, this doesn't make any sense.

731
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:29,080
Either I should know you or you should know me.

732
00:38:29,080 --> 00:38:31,160
Agreed. So why don't we?

733
00:38:31,160 --> 00:38:33,800
I don't know. Why don't you try asking that cute little gizmo of yours?

734
00:38:34,760 --> 00:38:35,880
Yeah, that's the one.

735
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:37,680
I did. I used it on you,

736
00:38:37,680 --> 00:38:39,640
but it couldn't decrypt the bio-shield.

737
00:38:39,640 --> 00:38:41,520
If you've been restored...

738
00:38:48,160 --> 00:38:49,320
Same person.

739
00:38:49,320 --> 00:38:52,600
Oh, no. But you don't recognise the sonic screwdriver.

740
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:54,080
Smart enough not to need one.

741
00:38:54,080 --> 00:38:56,960
Oh, yeah, nothing screams "smart" like a laser rifle.

742
00:38:57,000 --> 00:38:58,560
I stored that before hiding,

743
00:38:58,560 --> 00:39:01,720
cos I knew Gat would come one day, and now she has.

744
00:39:01,720 --> 00:39:03,000
Who is this Gat?

745
00:39:03,880 --> 00:39:05,720
I worked for her once.

746
00:39:05,720 --> 00:39:07,760
You've got a job? Oh, sort of.

747
00:39:07,760 --> 00:39:10,040
Not one you apply for. Not one you can ever leave.

748
00:39:10,040 --> 00:39:11,360
Believe me, I tried.

749
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:13,760
You've been hiding on Earth.

750
00:39:13,760 --> 00:39:17,720
You used the Chameleon Arch to hide your identity,

751
00:39:17,720 --> 00:39:20,440
to hide your mind, even from yourself.

752
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:22,160
That's why the sonic didn't pick it up!

753
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:23,880
And Lee was your protector.

754
00:39:23,880 --> 00:39:25,760
Well done.

755
00:39:25,800 --> 00:39:27,720
You're only five minutes behind someone who just had

756
00:39:27,760 --> 00:39:30,040
their memory fully restored. Five points!

757
00:39:30,040 --> 00:39:32,680
Don't do points, I do points. Points are my thing.

758
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:34,120
Oh!

759
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:36,920
What's happening?

760
00:39:37,920 --> 00:39:39,440
She's here.

761
00:39:42,360 --> 00:39:44,520
The Judoon have got us in a tractor beam,

762
00:39:44,520 --> 00:39:46,440
dragging us aboard their ship.

763
00:39:50,440 --> 00:39:53,440
Now listen to me, Doctor.

764
00:39:53,440 --> 00:39:55,280
Let me do the talking.

765
00:39:55,280 --> 00:39:57,440
Do not get involved.

766
00:39:57,440 --> 00:40:00,400
Because, if you really are me, and Gat figures that?

767
00:40:00,400 --> 00:40:02,160
She'll kill us both.

768
00:40:17,200 --> 00:40:19,760
Here we are, then. End of the road.

769
00:40:21,480 --> 00:40:24,080
I thought I'd be angry when I saw you.

770
00:40:25,680 --> 00:40:27,680
Turns out I'm just sorry.

771
00:40:27,680 --> 00:40:30,880
Not as sorry as I'm about to be.

772
00:40:30,880 --> 00:40:32,880
Ruth, put it down.

773
00:40:32,880 --> 00:40:36,000
Yes, "Ruth". Do as your little friend says.

774
00:40:36,720 --> 00:40:38,880
You are surrounded, after all.

775
00:40:51,200 --> 00:40:53,440
Don't point that thing at me, Gat.

776
00:40:53,440 --> 00:40:54,760
This was mine, you stole it.

777
00:40:54,760 --> 00:40:56,560
Mm, confiscated it.

778
00:40:57,680 --> 00:41:00,320
No, really, don't point it at me.

779
00:41:00,320 --> 00:41:01,840
Perfect for your execution.

780
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:03,440
I really wouldn't do that, Gat.

781
00:41:03,440 --> 00:41:05,440
Enough now. Let's get off this rust bucket

782
00:41:05,440 --> 00:41:06,480
and finish this on my ship.

783
00:41:06,480 --> 00:41:08,680
- When you say "finish this"? - Shut up.

784
00:41:08,680 --> 00:41:10,480
Take her advice, little woman.

785
00:41:10,480 --> 00:41:12,760
"Little"?

786
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:13,880
Biting my tongue.

787
00:41:13,880 --> 00:41:16,240
Contract states Judoon must deliver fugitive

788
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:18,280
to contractee at Division.

789
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:20,080
I'm here on behalf of the contractee!

790
00:41:20,080 --> 00:41:22,160
Hang on, I thought you'd hired the Judoon.

791
00:41:22,160 --> 00:41:23,360
- Who are you? - I'm...

792
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:24,840
Imperial Regulator.

793
00:41:24,840 --> 00:41:27,200
Sort of. Bit of a fib. Sorry.

794
00:41:27,200 --> 00:41:29,040
Actually, I'm... She's nobody.

795
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:31,720
Fine. I'm nobody.

796
00:41:31,720 --> 00:41:33,240
Absolutely nobody.

797
00:41:33,240 --> 00:41:34,520
See, I know why you want her,

798
00:41:34,520 --> 00:41:36,360
you've got a contract, fair enough. But you?

799
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:38,920
You want her dead because she left her job?

800
00:41:38,920 --> 00:41:41,480
- Shut up! - Is that what she told you?

801
00:41:42,840 --> 00:41:44,960
This goes way higher than me.

802
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,480
So, who would that be?

803
00:41:46,480 --> 00:41:48,560
Who are you all ultimately working for?

804
00:41:48,560 --> 00:41:50,760
I'd really like to know. Really.

805
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:52,680
Information confidential.

806
00:41:52,680 --> 00:41:54,960
I told you to keep quiet!

807
00:41:54,960 --> 00:41:56,280
And look where that's gotten us,

808
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:58,280
lots of guns in lots of faces.

809
00:41:58,280 --> 00:41:59,440
And have you got a better idea?

810
00:41:59,440 --> 00:42:01,880
I do, actually. My favourite,

811
00:42:01,880 --> 00:42:03,720
the curveball and the Judoon.

812
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:07,600
- You wanted to find The Doctor? - Don't you dare.

813
00:42:07,600 --> 00:42:10,360
- Well, here I am. - Will you be quiet?!

814
00:42:10,360 --> 00:42:12,560
Go on, scan me.

815
00:42:17,440 --> 00:42:19,440
Fugitive match positive.

816
00:42:21,720 --> 00:42:24,000
Fugitive match positive.

817
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:28,920
Is there even a word for how dumb you are?

818
00:42:28,920 --> 00:42:30,200
"Doctor"?

819
00:42:30,200 --> 00:42:32,760
Subsection 951 triggered.

820
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:35,760
Two fugitives, two payments.

821
00:42:35,800 --> 00:42:36,920
There won't be two payments,

822
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:38,280
because two of the same Time Lord

823
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:40,480
can't occupy the same space at the same time.

824
00:42:40,480 --> 00:42:43,360
It's an abomination! It'll destroy the time streams

825
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:45,520
before you get anywhere near Gallifrey!

826
00:42:45,520 --> 00:42:46,920
What did you say?

827
00:42:52,600 --> 00:42:54,600
Gallifreyan.

828
00:42:54,600 --> 00:42:56,080
You're from home.

829
00:42:56,080 --> 00:42:58,560
I serve for the glory of Gallifrey.

830
00:42:58,560 --> 00:43:00,840
Then both of you can only be my past.

831
00:43:02,520 --> 00:43:04,280
But that's impossible, because I know my own past,

832
00:43:04,320 --> 00:43:06,480
I lived through it. All of it.

833
00:43:06,480 --> 00:43:08,880
- You're wrong. - I'm not wrong!

834
00:43:08,880 --> 00:43:11,120
I've seen Gallifrey destroyed. Twice.

835
00:43:11,120 --> 00:43:15,280
First by a war, second by a lunatic who I'm still trying to find.

836
00:43:15,280 --> 00:43:19,000
In my time, Gallifrey doesn't exist.

837
00:43:20,040 --> 00:43:22,640
It's gone! Forever.

838
00:43:22,640 --> 00:43:26,120
And if you don't know that, you're in my past.

839
00:43:26,120 --> 00:43:29,440
So, you are only serving at the glory of ash and bone.

840
00:43:30,400 --> 00:43:31,680
This is a trick.

841
00:43:31,680 --> 00:43:34,880
Check my mind, one Time Lord to another.

842
00:43:34,880 --> 00:43:36,440
See what I saw.

843
00:43:37,880 --> 00:43:39,320
Keep an eye on her.

844
00:43:42,840 --> 00:43:43,880
Contact.

845
00:43:47,080 --> 00:43:48,320
What did you see?

846
00:43:51,560 --> 00:43:53,280
What did she show you?

847
00:43:53,960 --> 00:43:55,520
I don't know what trickery this is...

848
00:43:56,720 --> 00:43:58,360
Put the gun down, Gat.

849
00:43:58,360 --> 00:43:59,480
...but it ends here!

850
00:43:59,480 --> 00:44:01,320
Don't do this.

851
00:44:07,560 --> 00:44:09,160
You knew that would happen.

852
00:44:09,160 --> 00:44:10,560
You sabotaged the gun.

853
00:44:10,560 --> 00:44:13,240
I told her not to do it. I begged her not to fire.

854
00:44:13,240 --> 00:44:14,560
But you knew she would!

855
00:44:14,560 --> 00:44:16,680
Don't take the moral high ground with me.

856
00:44:16,680 --> 00:44:18,400
Crime has been witnessed.

857
00:44:18,400 --> 00:44:19,720
No crime.

858
00:44:19,720 --> 00:44:21,560
An accident.

859
00:44:21,560 --> 00:44:25,520
And, besides, a Judoonese Talwak Freighter like this,

860
00:44:25,520 --> 00:44:28,080
moving at 80 million clicks an hour,

861
00:44:28,080 --> 00:44:30,600
entered interstellar space...

862
00:44:30,600 --> 00:44:32,120
...12 seconds ago.

863
00:44:32,920 --> 00:44:38,160
No-one has jurisdiction in interstellar space.

864
00:44:38,160 --> 00:44:42,440
So, no laws, and no crime.

865
00:44:42,440 --> 00:44:44,280
Isn't that right, Doctor?

866
00:44:46,680 --> 00:44:48,200
Yes.

867
00:44:48,200 --> 00:44:50,520
Recalibrated.

868
00:44:50,520 --> 00:44:52,320
Who wants some?

869
00:44:52,320 --> 00:44:54,240
The Doctor never uses weapons.

870
00:44:54,240 --> 00:44:56,080
I know. Shut up!

871
00:44:57,120 --> 00:44:59,000
We're leaving now.

872
00:45:00,760 --> 00:45:05,200
If you know what's good for you, do not come for me again.

873
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:06,800
Ever.

874
00:45:06,800 --> 00:45:10,360
Consider your contract cancelled.

875
00:45:12,640 --> 00:45:15,280
Judoon contracts will always be fulfilled!

876
00:45:19,800 --> 00:45:22,120
Homing in near your TARDIS signal.

877
00:45:22,920 --> 00:45:24,800
Can't get too close.

878
00:45:24,800 --> 00:45:26,800
Imagine the temporal feedback loop.

879
00:45:28,600 --> 00:45:31,360
I'll drop you at the docks near my flat. How's that?

880
00:45:32,480 --> 00:45:33,960
You can't be me.

881
00:45:34,760 --> 00:45:36,800
I know what I've done, I know my own life.

882
00:45:36,800 --> 00:45:38,400
One of us has to be wrong.

883
00:45:46,000 --> 00:45:48,640
I'd quite like it if you got off my ship now.

884
00:45:51,720 --> 00:45:52,840
There she is!

885
00:45:53,880 --> 00:45:55,560
Doctor! Found you.

886
00:45:56,760 --> 00:45:59,160
Hey, what happened? Where you been?

887
00:45:59,160 --> 00:46:02,120
What happened to Ruth? The Judoon things are gone.

888
00:46:02,160 --> 00:46:03,600
You're never going to guess what happened to us.

889
00:46:03,640 --> 00:46:05,280
Captain Jack Harkness said hello.

890
00:46:05,280 --> 00:46:07,000
What?

891
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:09,080
"Beware the lone Cyberman.

892
00:46:09,080 --> 00:46:12,600
Do not let it have what it wants, at all costs."

893
00:46:12,600 --> 00:46:13,920
That's all he said?

894
00:46:13,920 --> 00:46:16,360
- Yeah, he got interrupted. - Who is he, anyway?

895
00:46:17,360 --> 00:46:19,000
An old friend.

896
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:20,120
I liked him.

897
00:46:20,120 --> 00:46:21,920
Kind of cheesy.

898
00:46:21,920 --> 00:46:24,040
But good cheesy.

899
00:46:24,040 --> 00:46:26,280
That's Jack.

900
00:46:26,280 --> 00:46:28,800
He didn't say any more about the Cybermen?

901
00:46:28,800 --> 00:46:31,160
Er, he said that they were a fallen empire

902
00:46:31,160 --> 00:46:32,760
and they should stay that way.

903
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:36,080
What are they, these Cybermen?

904
00:46:36,560 --> 00:46:38,720
They're one of the most dangerous species

905
00:46:38,720 --> 00:46:41,440
I've ever encountered, up there with the Daleks.

906
00:46:41,440 --> 00:46:43,600
Oh, I can't wait to meet then, then.

907
00:46:43,600 --> 00:46:45,240
And they're in our future?

908
00:46:45,280 --> 00:46:47,160
They're always somewhere...

909
00:46:48,560 --> 00:46:49,840
...waiting.

910
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:52,840
You haven't told us about Lee and Ruth and the Judoon.

911
00:46:53,720 --> 00:46:55,080
Who was the fugitive?

912
00:46:59,240 --> 00:47:00,400
It was Ruth.

913
00:47:02,040 --> 00:47:03,480
But Ruth was me.

914
00:47:04,360 --> 00:47:05,440
What?

915
00:47:06,480 --> 00:47:07,960
What are you talking about?

916
00:47:07,960 --> 00:47:09,440
How's that possible?

917
00:47:09,920 --> 00:47:13,520
She said she was my past, but I know my past,

918
00:47:13,520 --> 00:47:15,040
and she's never been me.

919
00:47:15,040 --> 00:47:17,040
I'm sure there's a simple explanation.

920
00:47:17,680 --> 00:47:20,560
Time is swirling around me.

921
00:47:20,560 --> 00:47:25,000
The Master, Captain Jack Harkness, Ruth.

922
00:47:27,440 --> 00:47:29,240
Something's coming for me.

923
00:47:30,400 --> 00:47:32,040
I can feel it.

924
00:47:32,040 --> 00:47:34,920
Let it come. You've got us.

925
00:47:34,960 --> 00:47:36,480
Ryan...

926
00:47:37,240 --> 00:47:40,640
...I've lived for thousands of years, so long I've lost count.

927
00:47:40,680 --> 00:47:43,600
I've had so many faces. How long have you been here?

928
00:47:45,040 --> 00:47:46,360
You don't know me.

929
00:47:47,320 --> 00:47:49,000
Not even a little bit.

930
00:47:49,000 --> 00:47:51,280
- Don't talk to him like that! - Yeah, I'm not having that.

931
00:47:51,280 --> 00:47:53,440
We do know who you are.

932
00:47:53,440 --> 00:47:55,640
You're the woman that brought us together,

933
00:47:55,640 --> 00:47:59,000
the woman that saved us and loads of other people.

934
00:48:02,840 --> 00:48:04,280
You're The Doctor.

935
00:48:06,640 --> 00:48:09,440
Whoever you were in the past or are in the future,

936
00:48:09,440 --> 00:48:11,960
we know who you are right now.

937
00:48:11,960 --> 00:48:14,040
- Right? - Right!

938
00:48:14,040 --> 00:48:16,040
The best person we know.

939
00:48:16,040 --> 00:48:19,520
And whatever is coming for you, we'll be here.

940
00:48:19,520 --> 00:48:21,040
Cos we're your mates.

941
00:48:21,080 --> 00:48:23,760
Well, not just mates. Family.

942
00:48:23,800 --> 00:48:24,840
- Yeah. - Yeah.

943
00:48:26,200 --> 00:48:28,840
So, whether you want to go looking

944
00:48:28,880 --> 00:48:30,320
for whatever trouble's coming,

945
00:48:30,360 --> 00:48:31,960
or whether you want to wait here

946
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:33,480
and let it come to you...

947
00:48:34,520 --> 00:48:36,920
...we'll be right here, by your side,

948
00:48:36,960 --> 00:48:39,560
like it or not, Doctor.

949
00:48:41,960 --> 00:48:43,520
What's that?

950
00:48:43,560 --> 00:48:44,840
I know what you're doing,

951
00:48:44,880 --> 00:48:46,760
siding with them, distracting me.

952
00:48:46,800 --> 00:48:48,760
You're doing this deliberately.

953
00:48:48,800 --> 00:48:50,680
Whoa!

954
00:48:50,720 --> 00:48:54,320
Multiple alerts across three continents here on Earth.

955
00:48:54,360 --> 00:48:57,040
Can't be connected. Unless they are.

956
00:48:57,040 --> 00:48:58,320
Quick look?

957
00:48:59,280 --> 00:49:00,640
Quick look.

958
00:49:01,720 --> 00:49:03,200
Let's go.

959
00:49:04,680 --> 00:49:06,680
Sync and corrections by btsix www.addic7ed.com

960
00:49:34,400 --> 00:49:36,320
Need some help over here!

961
00:49:36,360 --> 00:49:39,000
Two identical deaths on two different continents.

962
00:49:39,040 --> 00:49:41,040
It's even more dangerous than I thought.

963
00:49:42,640 --> 00:49:44,000
This can't be happening.

1
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,120
เหมาะสม.

2
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,600
โอ้!

3
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:08,120
ฉันบอกว่าฉันจะทำอาหารเช้าให้คุณเป็นวันเกิด

4
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:11,080
ใช่แล้ว ฉันหิวและคุณก็ตายจากโลกไปแล้ว

5
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,280
ขอโทษ.

6
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,120
ของขวัญเต็มรถบรรทุกน่าจะทดแทนสิ่งนั้นได้

7
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,240
- ใช่แล้ว เกี่ยวกับเรื่องนั้น... - ฉันล้อเล่นนะ!

8
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,280
- ไม่มีของขวัญ มีแต่เค้ก - ใช่

9
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:22,880
- คุณมีเค้กให้ฉันไหม? - ใช่ ฉันมีเค้กเต็มไปหมดเลย

10
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,040
อืม มีรูปแล้ว!

11
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:34,160
เอาล่ะ วันจันทร์ ทำสิ่งที่แย่ที่สุดของคุณซะ

12
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:35,440
- บาทหลวง - บาทหลวง

13
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:37,040
- ขอให้มีวันดีๆ นะ - ฉันจะทำ

14
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:56,680
ว้าว! คุณสบายดีไหมที่รัก?

15
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:58,600
สวัสดี! สวัสดี!

16
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,080
สวัสดีเจ้าหมา

17
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,040
- ขอแผ่นพับหน่อย - โอเค ขอบคุณครับ

18
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,360
- สวัสดีตอนเช้า ทานอันนี้สักแก้วนะ - ขอบคุณ

19
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:04,880
สวัสดี คุณสบายดีไหม?

20
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,920
สวัสดีตอนเช้า เรจจี้

21
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:18,400
สวัสดีตอนเช้าครับ เป็นครั้งแรกที่มากลอสเตอร์เหรอครับ

22
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,640
ลองทัวร์นำเที่ยวของฉันดูสิ

23
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,800
มาเมืองกลอสเตอร์ครั้งแรกเหรอ?

24
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:24,000
นี่เป็นครั้งแรกของคุณที่กลอสเตอร์หรือเปล่า? ลองทัวร์พร้อมไกด์ของฉันสิ!

25
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,960
นี่คือฉัน ลองทัวร์นำเที่ยวของฉันดูสิ

26
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,840
ฉันรู้ข้อเท็จจริงที่น่าตื่นเต้นทั้งหมดเกี่ยวกับเมืองกลอสเตอร์ ใช่ ฉันรู้

27
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,440
ทดสอบฉันสิ!

28
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,640
ไปต่อเลย

29
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:34,720
- บอกฉันอะไรหน่อย - โอเค

30
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:37,760
ในปี ค.ศ. 1216 มหาวิหารแห่งนี้เป็นเจ้าภาพจัดงาน

31
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,640
พิธีราชาภิเษกของพระเจ้าเฮนรี่ที่ 3

32
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,080
และเขาอายุเพียงเก้าขวบเท่านั้นในตอนนั้น!

33
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:46,080
ที่นี่เขาก็ถ่ายทำแฮรี่ พอตเตอร์ด้วย

34
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:49,320
ใช่แล้ว มีอีกมากมายที่มาจากที่นั่น

35
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,880
ทัวร์เริ่มเวลา 10.00 น., 12.00 น. และ 14.00 น.

36
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,400
ฉันจะ...คิดดูนะ

37
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,960
ใช่.

38
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:56,760
เธอจะไม่คิดถึงเรื่องนั้น

39
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,520
ไม่หรอกที่รัก เธอจะไม่ทำอย่างนั้น

40
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,440
เอาเถอะ ไม่เป็นไร

41
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:02,040
วันยังเด็กอยู่

42
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,400
มันหมายถึงเป็นหัวใจ

43
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,480
เอ่อ...ต้องปรับปรุงหน่อย

44
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:13,520
ฉันรู้ ผู้ชายใช้ชีวิตทั้งชีวิตอยู่หลังบาร์...

45
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:16,960
...การเปลี่ยนไปสู่การค้าร้านกาแฟไม่ใช่เรื่องง่าย แต่ฉันจะพยายาม

46
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,760
สำหรับคุณฉันจะลองทุกอย่าง

47
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,880
อัลลัน เราคุยกันเรื่องนี้แล้ว

48
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,880
โอ้ ฉันรู้ว่าคุณอยู่กับลี แต่คุณสมควรได้รับสิ่งที่ดีกว่านี้!

49
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:25,920
โอ้.

50
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:28,200
คุณรู้ว่ามีบางอย่างผิดปกติที่นั่น

51
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:32,640
นั่นคือเอกสารจริงใช่ไหม?

52
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:35,400
- ใช่แล้ว ลี แฟ้มลีของฉัน - โอ้ เอาเถอะน่า!

53
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,120
เขาแทบไม่คุยกับใครเลย...

54
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,800
...ตัดผมตัวเอง

55
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,800
นำหนังสือแปลกๆ ออกมาจากห้องสมุด

56
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,640
อ้างว่าครอบครัวของเขามาจากแถวนี้

57
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:44,400
แต่ฉันไม่สามารถหาใครที่รู้จักพวกเขาได้เลย

58
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,440
- คุณจะเชื่อใจได้ยังไง? - ขอบคุณสำหรับกาแฟวันเกิดของฉัน

59
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,360
รูธ ฉันบอกคุณแล้ว ฉันได้ยินอะไรบางอย่าง

60
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,600
พวกเขาไม่ได้เรียกฉันว่า Allan เพราะไม่มีอะไรเลย

61
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:55,240
ถ้าตั้งให้ตัวเองก็ไม่ใช่ชื่อเล่นใช่มั้ยล่ะ?

62
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:25,200
ฟรโล!

63
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
โบ โฟร โช โต!

64
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,480
ไม่โบโก้!

65
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,400
โมโลโซ!

66
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,840
ไม่มีโครโด!

67
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,520
เธอทำมันอีกแล้ว

68
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,120
ใช้เวลาหลายชั่วโมงที่ศูนย์ควบคุมเพื่อค้นหาบางสิ่งบางอย่าง

69
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,000
คิดว่าเราไม่ได้สังเกตเห็น

70
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,920
ฉันจะถามเธอ

71
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:04,560
เฮ้ หมอ คุณกำลังมองหาอะไรอยู่?

72
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,480
คุณอยู่ที่นั่นมานานแค่ไหนแล้ว?

73
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,720
20 นาที

74
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,280
คุณไม่ได้

75
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,360
คุณกำลังมองหาอะไรอยู่?

76
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,640
ไม่ได้มองหาอะไรเลย

77
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:14,120
อย่าโกหกเรา

78
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,000
พระอาจารย์.

79
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,720
ทำไมคุณถึงทำอย่างนั้น?

80
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,680
- กาสะวินเอาเขาไป - ใช่.

81
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,120
พวกเขาพาเขาไปยังมิติของพวกเขา

82
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,480
และฉันไม่สามารถไปที่นั่นใน TARDIS ได้ แต่ฉันคิดว่า...

83
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,360
...ถ้าเขาหนีออกมาได้ ฉันก็ติดตามเขาได้

84
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:33,280
ไม่มีสัญญาณอะไรเลย

85
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:35,640
ฉันคิดว่าเขาจะเป็นคนสุดท้ายที่คุณอยากเจอ

86
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,600
เขาฝากข้อความไว้สำหรับฉัน

87
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,440
พูดอะไรนะ?

88
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,840
มันเป็นเรื่องส่วนตัว

89
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:46,960
นั่นคือที่ที่คุณไปเหรอ?

90
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,560
เมื่อคุณทิ้งเราให้สำรวจและคุณพูดว่า

91
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,640
คุณจะกลับมาในอีกหนึ่งชั่วโมงแต่คุณไม่เคยกลับมาเลยเหรอ?

92
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,120
คุณออกไปตามหาเขาเหรอ?

93
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,640
คุณจะไปไหน?

94
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,760
บ้าน.

95
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,600
ด้วยตัวฉันเอง

96
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,600
ทำไม? ทำไมไม่ใช่กับเราล่ะ?

97
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:22,600
เพราะคุณถามคำถามมากเกินไป

98
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,600
บางทีอาจเป็นเพราะเราเป็นห่วงคุณ?

99
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,840
ฉันหมายถึงว่านาทีหนึ่งคุณก็ยิ้มแย้ม

100
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,720
นาทีถัดไปจิตใจของคุณก็ไปที่อื่น

101
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:33,880
Kro Kro Tro Kro เทียวไปเทียวมา!

102
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,880
- โคร โคร โทร โคร... - นั่นอะไรน่ะ?

103
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,840
การส่งสัญญาณเตือนภัยของจูดูน

104
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:40,600
แก้ม!

105
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,960
จูดูนเหรอ?

106
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:43,520
คุณแค่พูดเพื่อให้เราเงียบใช่ไหม?

107
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:46,080
ตำรวจนอกจักรวาลอันตรายรับจ้าง

108
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:50,120
ประกาศ...เกี่ยวกับสนามบังคับใช้โซนบนโลก

109
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,800
ไม่มีใครสามารถเข้าหรือออกได้

110
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:55,680
อะไรนะ? เขากำลังเตรียมบีมลงไปตรงนั้น

111
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:58,120
กองร้อยของจูดูน ใกล้ดวงจันทร์

112
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,720
พวกเขาทำแบบนั้นไม่ได้หรอก พวกเขาไม่มีอำนาจศาลที่นั่น

113
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:04,040
ใจกลางเมืองกลอสเตอร์เลย! ฉันจะไม่เอาแบบนั้นเด็ดขาด!

114
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:06,400
หากฉันสามารถจับคู่การหมุนของ TARDIS ได้

115
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:09,600
ตามความถี่ของอัตราการรีเฟรชของสนามบังคับใช้

116
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:10,800
ฉันอาจจะสามารถ

117
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,600
เพื่อลักลอบพาเราเข้าไปก่อนที่ใครจะโดนฆ่า

118
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,040
ฉันคิดว่าคุณบอกว่าพวกเขาเป็นตำรวจ

119
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,960
ตำรวจที่ชอบใช้อาวุธบ่อย

120
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:26,680
โดโปโลโช!

121
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,920
ไม่ดรอปโฟโร! โซ!

122
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,160
ทู โฟ โร!

123
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,840
โก โร โฟร!

124
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:42,840
โบ.

125
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:45,680
ไปแล้ว!

126
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,200
โซ โซ โร!

127
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,880
ทูโชโฟร!

128
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,600
โซโซโต!

129
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,600
โนโฟโล!

130
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,840
โนโฟโล!

131
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,920
โน โฟ โบ โบ โล!

132
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,320
โร!

133
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:14,920
วิล โร โคร ทู ฟโร วิล! โซ!

134
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:18,160
- มาร์เซีย อย่า! - คุณกล้าดียังไง!

135
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:22,120
นี่เป็นเมืองเล็กๆ ที่เงียบสงบ แล้วคุณเป็นใครกัน?

136
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,080
โทรโก้โช.

137
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,920
นั่นใช้เวลาฉันเก้าสัปดาห์

138
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,160
นั่นใช้เวลาฉันเก้าสัปดาห์

139
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,800
ภาษามนุษย์.

140
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,680
นี่มันอะไร?

141
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,760
การชดเชยสำหรับอาวุธของคุณ

142
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,560
ตอบคำถามของเธอ!

143
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,080
คุณเป็นใคร?

144
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,800
พวกเราคือ...

145
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:44,280
...จูดูน

146
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:49,000
โอ้...พระเจ้า...

147
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,600
คุณจะถูกจัดทำรายการ

148
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:53,520
ฉันจะไม่! อยู่ห่างๆ ฉันไว้!

149
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,280
ไม่นะ! มาร์เซีย!

150
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:01,600
ขอบเขตสนามบังคับใช้กฎหมายมีความแข็งแกร่งสูงสุด

151
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,840
คุณฆ่าเธอ!

152
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:06,280
หมวดหมู่ มนุษย์.

153
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,160
แมทช์หนีตาย ลบ.

154
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:13,040
- คุณต้องการอะไรจากเรา - ทั้งหมดภายในขอบเขต

155
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:16,480
ต้องจัดทำรายการไว้ ผู้หลบหนีอยู่ที่นี่

156
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,200
อ้าว ดูสิว่าไม่ใช่ใคร...!

157
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,640
ฉันมาเอาเค้ก

158
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:25,600
ที่ฉันสั่งไว้สำหรับวันเกิดของรูธ

159
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,680
โอ้ เข้าใจแล้วที่นี่

160
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:28,760
ข้อความวันเกิดพิเศษถึงเธอ

161
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:36,320
เป็นอะไรไปคะ ทำไมไม่ปล่อยไปล่ะคะ

162
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,520
คุณอยากจะเอาสิ่งนี้ออกไปข้างนอกใช่ไหม?

163
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:38,520
หยุดถามฉันแบบนั้น

164
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:40,760
ทุกครั้งที่ฉันมาที่นี่เพื่อดื่มลาเต้!

165
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,600
มนุษย์!

166
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:45,600
- ตรงนี้นะ - คุณมาทำอะไรในครัวของฉัน!

167
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:48,360
อยู่ข้างใน ปิดประตูไว้ อย่าให้ใครเข้ามา

168
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:51,200
โดยเฉพาะตำรวจเอเลี่ยนที่สวมหมวกกันน็อคและชุดหนังสีดำ

169
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:54,720
เมืองกำลังถูกปิดล้อม เราจะจัดการมัน

170
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:58,360
โอ้ ใช่ ไปเลย ออกไปซะ ไอ้ขี้ขลาด!

171
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:00,240
- เขาเป็นอะไรไป? - คุณมีเวลาอีกนานแค่ไหน?

172
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:02,840
ไม่มีเวลาเลย อยู่ข้างใน ล็อคประตูซะ

173
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:04,160
เอาล่ะเพื่อนๆ ไม่มีเวลาแล้ว

174
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:07,560
เปล่าๆ เพื่อนๆ ดูพวกอันน้อยนี้สิ

175
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:08,680
น่ารัก!

176
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,080
ดูสภาพมันสิ!

177
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,640
นั่นเป็นเค้กที่แย่ที่สุดที่ฉันเคยเห็น!

178
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,320
รูธ ฉันตามหาคุณทุกที่แล้ว

179
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,600
- คุณเคยเห็นไหม? - ใช่.

180
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,880
- พวกมันเป็นมนุษย์ต่างดาว! - ฉันรู้ ฉันรู้

181
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:23,120
มนุษย์ต่างดาวตัวจริง พวกมันฆ่ามาร์เซีย

182
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,320
- อะไรนะ? - มาร์เซียตายแล้ว

183
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,560
เราต้องกลับบ้านเดี๋ยวนี้

184
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:31,360
แรดอวกาศเหรอ?

185
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,560
ฉันไม่มีเงินเลย ขอโทษนะ ฉันทำงานนี้ไม่เก่งเลย

186
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:38,880
หมวดหมู่ มนุษย์. การจับคู่ผู้หลบหนี, ลบ.

187
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,280
โอ้ คุณกำลังตามล่าผู้หลบหนีอยู่เหรอ?

188
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,760
ฉันช่วยได้ เขาเพิ่งจากไป

189
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:44,200
บนเคาน์เตอร์มีเอกสารอยู่

190
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,360
มันละเอียดจริงๆ

191
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:51,240
เฮ้ย! ระวังหน่อยไอ้...ไอ้โง่!

192
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:56,320
ขอโทษ.

193
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,480
การทำร้ายร่างกายเจ้าหน้าที่

194
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,720
ประโยค, การดำเนินการ

195
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,920
ประโยคสมบูรณ์แล้ว!

196
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,600
ตกลง.

197
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:08,880
ต้องหยิบของจำเป็น เสื้อผ้าอีกนิดหน่อย เราต้องไปแล้ว

198
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,680
คุณกำลังพูดเรื่องอะไร ไปไหน?

199
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:12,120
คุณเชื่อใจฉันไหม รูธ?

200
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,120
บางครั้ง.

201
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:16,240
คุณต้องทำตามที่ฉันบอก

202
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:18,240
เพียงแค่หยิบเสื้อผ้าแล้วใส่ลงในกระเป๋าเดินทาง

203
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,640
พวกมันตามคุณมาไม่ได้หรอก พวกมันเป็นมนุษย์ต่างดาว

204
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:22,440
พวกมันมีหัวเหมือนแรด

205
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:24,160
คุณมาจากสตรูด ลี

206
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,960
หากมีสิ่งใดที่ฉันจำเป็นต้องรู้

207
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,840
คุณบอกฉันตอนนี้เลย

208
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,800
ไม่มีเวลาแล้ว รีบมาเถอะ

209
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:43,160
ตั้งอยู่หน่วยบ้านผู้หลบหนี

210
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,600
เตรียมเครื่องแยกไอโซเลเตอร์

211
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:46,720
ฉันหวังว่าคุณจะมีใบอนุญาตสำหรับเรื่องนั้นแล้ว

212
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:48,720
คุณเป็นผู้ควบคุมจักรวรรดิใช่ไหม?

213
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:51,440
ใช่ครับ และที่นี่ก็มีเรื่องที่ต้องควบคุมมากมาย

214
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,760
สำหรับผู้เริ่มต้น คุณไม่มีอำนาจศาลที่นี่

215
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:57,080
แล้วทำไมคุณถึงใช้สนามบังคับใช้คลาส 7

216
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:59,080
รอบๆ เมืองนี้ทำให้ฉันกังวลมาก

217
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,840
ที่สำคัญกว่านั้น ตัวแยกชั่วคราวนี้

218
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,680
เป็นอุปกรณ์ที่ผิดกฎหมาย

219
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:06,720
การรั่วไหลของรังสีและความสูญเสียของพลเรือน

220
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,200
ออกแบบมาเพื่อหยุดเวลาแต่ทำให้เกิด

221
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,480
ความเสียหายอันเลวร้ายต่อทุกสิ่งทุกอย่างและทุกคน

222
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,400
ที่ขวางทางมัน น่ากลัวจริงๆ

223
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,120
เฮ้ คุณไม่ได้ใช้สิ่งนั้นที่นี่นะเพื่อน

224
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:16,840
ดังนั้น ให้ถือว่าก้นแรดของคุณได้รับการควบคุมอย่างเข้มงวด

225
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,760
มันฟังดูยากขึ้นในหัวฉัน

226
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:23,560
